INT. WESTFIELD HIGH SCHOOL - BOYS' BATHROOM - DAY

ON CAMERA: handheld, shaky, filming through a gap between two stalls. Fluorescent hum. A dripping tap.

Sam, 17, leans on the sink, phone in hand, in a hoodie. Next to him, Mo, 17, washes his hands for far too long.

The documentary crew is not supposed to be here. They are here anyway.

SAM
(to camera, quiet)
You said you wouldn't film this part.

MO
Turn it off. Seriously.

The tap runs. Nobody turns anything off.

This is the last time they will all be in the same room before the hearing.

A stall door SLAMS. Big Dave, 18, steps out, shoulders filling the frame.

BIG DAVE
Who's talking? Who's talking about me?

SAM
Nobody.

MO
We're not.

JEN
(from the doorway, a girl in a blazer, clipboard clutched)
You're all still here? The hearing's in ten minutes.

BIG DAVE
You think I don't know that?

SAM
Jen, you shouldn't be in here.

JEN
Mrs. K said to find you.

MO
She said what?

BIG DAVE
She said it's fine, they said it's fine, it's all fine.

JEN
Nobody said it's fine, Dave.

SAM
Can we just

MO
Let her finish.

JEN
The statement has to match. Word for word. If one of you changes one thing.

BIG DAVE
I'm not changing anything.

MO
You already did. You said it was a door.

BIG DAVE
It WAS a door.

SAM
It wasn't a door, man.

JEN
Stop. Everyone stop.

The phone BUZZES in Sam's hand. He stares at it.

MRS. K (O.S.)
(through the door)
Samuel? Time.

Nobody moves. The tap drips. Sam sets the phone on the sink, face down.

SAM
(barely a whisper)
I'm telling them.
